      "problem": "Solve the equation  $6x^2 +2x -2= 8x^2- x -2.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+2x-2 & =8{x}^{2}-x-2 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+2x-2-(8{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+2x-2-8{x}^{2}+x+2 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-8{x}^{2})+(2x+x)+(-2+2) & =0 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+3x+0 & =0 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ x(-2x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by the zero product rule, we have\n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad -2x + 3=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives \n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad x=\\dfrac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=0,\\dfrac{3}{2}.$",
